# 🍷 Wine Quality Prediction Using Machine Learning

## 📌 Project Overview

This project focuses on predicting wine quality using Machine Learning classification algorithms. The analysis is performed on the Red Wine Quality dataset, which contains different physicochemical properties of red wine.

The project involves data exploration, statistical analysis, data visualization, quality categorization, model training, prediction, and performance evaluation.

Three Machine Learning algorithms are implemented and compared to identify the best-performing model for wine quality classification.

This project is completed as part of the **Oasis Infobyte Internship (OIBSIP) – Data Analytics, Level 2, Task 2**.

## 🎯 Project Objectives

- Understand and explore the Red Wine Quality dataset.
- Perform data inspection and statistical analysis.
- Analyze the distribution of wine quality scores.
- Identify relationships between chemical properties and wine quality.
- Visualize feature distributions and correlations.
- Convert numerical quality scores into Low, Medium, and High categories.
- Train multiple Machine Learning classification models.
- Evaluate and compare model performance.
- Identify the best-performing classification algorithm.

## 📂 Dataset Information

**Dataset Name:** `winequality-red.csv`

**Dataset Size:** 1,599 rows and 12 columns.

The dataset contains physicochemical properties of red wine and its corresponding quality score.

### Dataset Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| fixed acidity | Amount of fixed acids in wine |
| volatile acidity | Amount of volatile acids |
| citric acid | Citric acid content |
| residual sugar | Amount of residual sugar |
| chlorides | Chloride concentration |
| free sulfur dioxide | Free sulfur dioxide content |
| total sulfur dioxide | Total sulfur dioxide content |
| density | Density of the wine |
| pH | Acidity or alkalinity level |
| sulphates | Sulphate concentration |
| alcohol | Alcohol percentage |
| quality | Wine quality score (target variable) |

