## 🔍 Project Workflow

### 1. Data Loading and Exploration

- Imported Pandas and NumPy.
- Loaded the Red Wine Quality dataset.
- Examined dataset dimensions and column names.
- Checked data types and statistical information.

### 2. Data Inspection

- Checked missing values.
- Examined numerical data types.
- Analyzed wine quality score distribution.
- Identified class imbalance in the target variable.

### 3. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)

Performed the following visualizations:

- Wine quality distribution count plot.
- Chemical feature distribution histograms.
- Correlation heatmap.
- Quality category distribution plot.

### 4. Quality Categorization

Converted numerical wine quality scores into three categories:

| Quality Score | Category |
|---|---|
| 3–4 | Low |
| 5–6 | Medium |
| 7–8 | High |

This categorization transforms the original numerical quality scores into a multiclass classification problem.

### 5. Feature Selection

- Selected 11 physicochemical features as input variables.
- Used `quality_category` as the target variable.
- Excluded the original quality score from the input features.

### 6. Train-Test Split

- Divided the dataset into training and testing sets.
- Used 80% of the data for training.
- Used 20% of the data for testing.
- Applied stratified sampling to maintain class distribution.
- Used `random_state=42`.

### 7. Machine Learning Model Building

Implemented three classification algorithms:

**Random Forest Classifier**
- Used 100 decision trees.
- Applied balanced class weights.
- Used the model to classify wine quality categories.

**SGD Classifier**
- Applied StandardScaler for feature scaling.
- Used Stochastic Gradient Descent.
- Applied balanced class weights.

**Support Vector Classifier (SVC)**
- Used an RBF kernel.
- Applied StandardScaler.
- Used balanced class weights.

### 8. Model Evaluation

Evaluated the models using:

- Accuracy Score
- Precision Score
- Recall Score
- F1 Score
- Confusion Matrix
- Classification Report

Macro-averaged Precision, Recall, and F1 Score were used to compare performance across all three quality categories.

## 📊 Model Performance Comparison

The following results were obtained from the notebook:

| Model | Accuracy | Precision | Recall | F1 Score |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Random Forest | 83.75% | 57.09% | 57.04% | 55.06% |
| SGD Classifier | 77.81% | 48.49% | 48.00% | 47.89% |
| SVC | 70.94% | 47.12% | 56.74% | 48.92% |

<text weight="semibold">Best Performing Model: Random Forest Classifier</text>

